  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, scgpt+resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.525 acc, a large jump over config_001 (image_only, resnet50, avgpool) at 0.328 acc. This confirms adding RNA helps, but we cannot yet decompose how much of the gain comes from the RNA signal itself versus the image-RNA fusion. Uncertainty: We do not know the standalone RNA contribution. If scgpt alone (config_009: rna_only, scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) already approaches ~0.50, the image modality adds little and future effort should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation. If it is much lower (~0.30-0.40), the image modality is essential and we should prioritize image encoder and fusion improvements. This is a clean ablation of config_008 (same RNA encoder, profile, aggregation; only the image modality and fusion are removed), making it the single most informative next experiment to reduce fundamental uncertainty about modality contribution before committing budget to narrower questions like fusion type or image encoder choice."
}

